          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Influence on Physics and Mathematics</strong><br>\nWitten's influence extends beyond his own discoveries. He has contributed to physics by providing new tools and methods that have become standard in the field. His work has also had a profound impact on modern mathematics, leading to the development of new areas of mathematical research inspired by theoretical physics.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Philosophy and Science Perspective</strong><br>\nApart from his scientific achievements, Witten has expressed his thoughts on the philosophy of science, especially regarding the nature of mathematical truth and its relationship to physics. He believes that the beauty and simplicity found in physical theories are a guide to understanding nature, suggesting a deep connection between the universe's workings and the elegance of mathematical structures.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy and Ongoing Work</strong><br>\nWitten continues to work at the forefront of theoretical physics, and his legacy is that of a trailblazer who has significantly broadened the scope of both mathematics and physics. His ongoing research may one day help answer some of the most profound questions about the origins of the universe, the fundamental forces that shape it, and the ultimate theory of everything.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
